{{also|Leben|lében}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|-}} and {{inh|de|goh|lebēn}}, from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*libbjan}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*libjaną}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*leyp-||leave, cling, linger}}. 

Cognate with {{cog|osx|libbian}} ({{cog|gml|leven}}, {{cog|nds-de|lęven}}, {{m|nds-de|lewen||to live}}), {{cog|nl|leven}}, {{cog|en|live}}, {{cog|fy|libje}}, {{cog|non|lifa}} ({{cog|sv|leva}}), {{cog|got|𐌻𐌹𐌱𐌰𐌽}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈleːbən/|[ˈleːbm̩]|[ˈleːb(ə)n]}}
* {{audio|de|De-leben.ogg|audio}}
* {{audio|de|De-at-Leben.ogg|audio (Austria)}}

===Verb===
{{de-verb}}

# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[live]], to be [[alive]]
# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[dwell]], to [[reside]]
#* '''2010''', ''{{w|Der Spiegel}}'', issue [http://www.spiegel.de/spiegel/print/index-2010-35.html 35/2010], page 102:
#*: {{quote|de|Es '''leben''' etwa 300 000 Bürger des ehemaligen Jugoslawien in der Schweiz, kaum ein Staat hat damals im Verhältnis zu seiner Einwohnerzahl so viele Flüchtlinge aufgenommen.|There '''are''' (reside) about 300,000 citizens of the former Yugoslavia living in Switzerland, hardly any state took in so many refugees in relation to its population at that time.}}
#: {{uxi|de|Ich '''lebe''' in der Schillerstraße in der Nähe des Stadtzentrums.|I '''live''' in the Schiller-street near the city's center.}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive}} to [[live]], to [[exist]], to occupy a place
#: {{uxi|de|Die Dinosaurier '''lebten''' für Jahrmillionen auf der Erde bevor der Mensch erschien.|The dinosaurs '''existed''' on Earth for millions of years prior to the rise of man.}}
# {{lb|de|intransitive|hyperbole}} to [[cope]] with, to [[live]] with, to [[deal]] with
#: {{uxi|de|Du wirst wohl damit '''leben''' müssen!|You'll have to '''cope with''' it!}}
#: {{uxi|de|Jeder muss mit seinen eigenen Problemen '''leben'''!|Everybody has to '''deal''' with his own issues.}}

